# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Line endings.
#
# This repository is edited on Windows (Git Bash / MobaXterm) and executed on a
# Linux HPC cluster (davinci-1, PBS). Git's default on Windows is
# core.autocrlf=true, which rewrites LF to CRLF on checkout. For .py that is
# merely untidy -- Python 3 accepts universal newlines -- but for the four shell
# scripts in this repo (Main/install_env.sh, Main/run_wiring_checks.sh,
# Main/hpc/sweep_threads.sh, Main/hpc/launch_4c_factorial.sh) it is FATAL: bash
# reads the trailing CR as part of the command and fails with the classic
#
#     $'\r': command not found
#     /bin/bash^M: bad interpreter: No such file or directory
#
# and qsub rejects the job. Declaring eol=lf here OVERRIDES core.autocrlf for
# every clone on every machine, so nobody has to remember to configure it.
#
# This is the same ASCII-first reasoning as the source-encoding rule: make the
# bytes on disk correct BY CONSTRUCTION rather than by convention, so that no
# transfer through a Windows tool can corrupt them.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
* text=auto eol=lf

*.py    text eol=lf
*.sh    text eol=lf
*.json  text eol=lf
*.md    text eol=lf
*.txt   text eol=lf
*.cfg   text eol=lf
*.yml   text eol=lf
*.yaml  text eol=lf

# Never let Git touch these.
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.pdf   binary
*.pt    binary
*.pth   binary
*.npz   binary
*.npy   binary
*.zip   binary
*.pkl   binary
